# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is a *per-machine* setting, so a clean history depends on every
# clone being configured correctly. This moves that guarantee into the repo,
# where it travels with the code — JB772/ai-full-stack is public, and the first
# CRLF file committed by a differently-configured clone lands as a whole-file
# diff that is tedious to unpick.
#
# Verified 2026-07-17 before adding: all 292 tracked text files were already LF
# in the index (0 with CRLF), so this normalizes nothing and produces no diff.
# That is why it was cheap to add now; the cost only rises once a CRLF file is in.
#
# Working trees are unaffected: Windows checkouts still get CRLF via autocrlf.
# Only what Git stores is pinned to LF.
* text=auto

# Binary — never normalize line endings, never diff as text.
# The fonts are 11.5 MB of OTF; a botched text conversion would corrupt them
# silently (see TODOS P2 on the Noto Sans TC payload).
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
